# Android build environment

This project is a legacy Android/Gradle project. Before attempting a Gradle
build in Cursor Cloud, set up the environment as follows:

Set up this Android project to build with Gradle 4.10.1: install
Temurin/OpenJDK 8, Android SDK platform 28, build-tools 28.0.3, platform-tools,
accept Android SDK licenses, and expose JAVA_HOME plus Android SDK path for
cloud agents.

Important details:

- Use JDK 8 for Gradle builds. The current Gradle/Kotlin/KAPT stack is not
  compatible with JDK 21.
- Install Android SDK platform `android-28`, build-tools `28.0.3`, and
  `platform-tools`.
- Accept Android SDK licenses before running Gradle.
- Set `JAVA_HOME` to the JDK 8 location when building.
- Set `ANDROID_HOME` or create an ignored `local.properties` with
  `sdk.dir=<android-sdk-path>`.
- Use `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug --no-daemon` for debug build verification.
